TEXT 368 -256 Left 2 ;Rkessel =  so that X0 should be between 3*X1 ... 10*X1 like\nin the transformer literature \nHere X1=Xk=1.28ohm\nSee also the wxmaxima file in this folder -> transformer_400V_400V.wxmx
TEXT 400 -664 Left 2 ;If you know X0 of your YY transformer\nyou can change rkessel (default=1e20) \nto a appropriate value so that your X0 is the simulation result\nAt 1e20 (default)  the magnetic kettleflow is not considered\nHINT: You can see that not only the value of X0 but also\nthe shape of the inrush currents is determined by the kettleflow.\nTherefore for accurate simulation it is important to set rkessel\nto a better value as 1e20
